WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:17.053
Access policies protect confidential software by deciding who
may obtain its decryption keys. Use a policy when a release
contains proprietary code or should only be readable by approved
devices. Start by creating a policy with a recognizable name.

2
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:31.093
Choose Group and select the devices’ group, then grant access
and approve the request. Current group membership is used when
devices request keys. You can reuse the policy for releases
intended for the same audience.

3
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:48.397
Revoking access stops future key requests. It cannot take back
software or keys that a device has already received. Review
group membership and grants before publishing sensitive
software, and keep deployment targeting aligned with the devices
that have access.

